# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1`
- Installed via: `npm install @vercel/analytics`
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` accordingly

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the JSX return statement
- Follows React/Vite framework-specific instructions from official Vercel documentation

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to `App.jsx` (the root application component) rather than `main.jsx` to ensure it renders within the React component tree and has access to the React Router context. This placement is ideal for tracking page views across all routes.

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation pattern for React/Vite applications:
```jsx
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";

function App() {
  return (
    <>
      {/* app content */}
      <Analytics />
    </>
  );
}
```

## Verification

✅ **Build**: Successfully builds without errors (`npm run build`)
✅ **Linting**: No new linting errors introduced in App.jsx
✅ **Tests**: No test suite configured in this project
✅ **Lock Files**: package-lock.json updated correctly

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Navigate to the Analytics section in your Vercel Dashboard
2. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
3. Analytics data will start appearing after a few days of visitors
4. Verify tracking by checking the browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

## Notes

- No environment variables required - the package automatically detects the Vercel environment upon deployment
- The Analytics component respects privacy and compliance standards
- Pre-existing linting errors in `TransactionForm.jsx` and `TransactionsContext.jsx` remain unchanged (not related to this implementation)
